{"success": true, "name": "arc-grid-reasoning", "file": "references/session-specific-mistakes.md", "content": "# Session-specific mistake pattern: unsupported placement guesses

A demonstrated input had a uniform field interrupted by a full-width colored row and a small marker object. The test used a full-width row plus a two-cell marker elsewhere. Repeatedly guessing which row should receive the demo's additional full-width color, while moving that row up or down, did not follow from the demonstration and produced repeated incorrect submissions. The demo alone did not uniquely establish the test placement rule. In this situation, request another example rather than treating arbitrary candidate coordinates as competing evidence-backed hypotheses. Preserve original test cells unless a validated rule entails their transformation.

Generalizable lesson: negative feedback is only whole-grid rejection, not a hint about the guessed coordinate. Stop positional/color cycling, reconstruct candidate rules from all demos, and seek information when the current evidence underdetermines the output.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1792545591/attempts/c7065a7854b1495da12b5b9aafb915a0/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/arc-grid-reasoning/references/session-specific-mistakes.md"}

